 "text": "Hey, good to have you here. How are you? Lovely. A rental hall with a nice cafe downstairs is the classic start. Then lake water is the main challenge. In summer, it' too warm for everyone except the youngest kids. In winter, it can be cold. Ask everyone who' be there and what they like. Some folks hate halls and want hotel room, others have small one. Think about refreshments. A sandwich board can't keep up with sandwiches and drinks. Would you do the kitchen, or just order in? Keep them simple. An opening game before the hall, and closing music if people bring instruments. Lots of sitting together is the main thing.",
